    "created_at": "2020-09-21T21:28:00Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-09-21T21:28:00Z",
    "body": "/cc @josepharhar. This is the bug I was referencing in https://bugs.chromium.org/p/chromium/issues/detail?id=591605#c16 about how one of the tests in https://wpt.fyi/results/html/infrastructure/common-dom-interfaces/collections/htmlallcollection.html?label=master&label=experimental&aligned&q=htmlallcollection fails in all browsers.\r\n\r\nI can't tell at a glance what Chromium's EnsureCachedCollection does; is it GC-dependent, or is it like Gecko and it will just grow the cache for as long as the document lives? Honestly neither of those sound great, so maybe browsers would like to align themselves with the test and always return a new collection? Or we just accept that this is an old legacy API and don't sink too much time into it until someone actually complains of an interop issue...",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
