    "created_at": "2020-09-21T23:23:49Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-09-21T23:34:22Z",
    "body": "Yeah. The test is checking that `document.all[\"foo\"] !== document.all.namedItem(\"foo\")` and various other checks. (It's not checking that multiple calls to the same access method return different values, i.e. there's no test for `document.all[\"foo\"] !== document.all[\"foo\"]`. That might be good to add; it's what the spec requires currently.)\r\n\r\nHowever, browsers cache them so that any query for `\"foo\"` will return the same `HTMLCollection`. This spec bug is opened to track the fact that the spec/tests mismatch browser behavior.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
